  "unique_targets": [
    {
      "block_id": "B0087",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "23030f518a91",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The frozen audit trail has an immutable repository locator:\\newline"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0123",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "ad4ad7c72508",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Data, materials, and code availability.}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0026",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "231a6b4c1b49",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The control's nonarithmeticity remains a bounded multi-source and inherited-project input. Takeuchi (1975)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0036",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "21389545e66a",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Strohmaier and Uski (2013, corrected 2018)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0044",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "9714c4b0ddf6",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Correction and locator boundaries were carried forward exactly. The Takeuchi record retains its correction binding (Takeuchi, 1975)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0067",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "e226039d3f69",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The literature supports the three-package architecture only at component and precedent level. Voight (2009)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0107",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "dedce0ac4fc8",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Third, bibliographic source-status work remains open. The S03 and S16 corrections are preserved as manuscript bindings, and the corrected S12 pages 287--305 rem"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0061",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "abf5b53a56d8",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The independent-validator contract remains prospective. Its trust graph has producer nodes BP and CP, adapter nodes \\(A_{\\mathrm{BP}}\\) and \\(A_{\\mathrm{CP}}\\),"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0072",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "6a60496cf945",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Package C makes those rules checkable by a party that does not trust producer summaries. Independence here is architectural: the validator derives acceptance fr"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0108",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "686299793396",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Fourth, the architecture is unimplemented. Neither producer has a frozen exact representation or theorem-applicability proof. No schema bytes, proof registry, v"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "ba435a21ed08",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Canonical records use UTF-8 in NFC form, no byte-order mark, LF line endings, byte-lexicographically ordered object keys, prescribed array order, and no insigni"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0059",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "c1201f6b9f62",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The paper-level common contract is \\path{P33-OWNER-CERT/1} with proof registry \\path{P33-PROOF-TYPES/1}. Its closed allowed top-level field set is \\path{schema_"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0062",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "bac5109800ae",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Fixtures must include accepted minimal records and rejected malformed schemas, unknown proof types, altered digests, unsupported negative decisions, primitive/p"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0128",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "fad762064c89",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The following manuscript-local traces are synthetic conformance examples, not surface records, executable fixture files, validator runs, or census outcomes. In "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "452573d2ac85",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\textbf{Surface-specific population-completeness procedure.} The prospective BP contract must consume the exact source-locked Bolza presentation in \\path{papers"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "3cca919f4b69",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\textbf{Control proof producer (CP).} CP would consume the source-locked control and the same semantic locks, but may use different number representations and p"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0015",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "cfe8ae896686",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The two project objects originate in a substantial but heterogeneous literature. Nazarenko (2013)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0025",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "173e02e1eb10",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The control is the single source-locked object \\texttt{NAZARENKO-EXP-OCTAGON-G2}, not a representative of all nonarithmetic surfaces. Nazarenko (2013)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0027",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "a9417c34e6c7",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The target is similarly treated through bounded complementary context. Aurich et al.~(1991)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0029",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "a198b5981f00",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Candidate generation and ownership require different proof objects. Aurich et al.~(1991)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0030",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "c06ca91759a8",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Primitive and reciprocal semantics must also remain distinct. Cherubini et al.~(2022)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0032",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "32208669ff00",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The frozen corpus contains strong component-level algorithmic precedents but no finished cross-surface implementation. Voight (2009)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0033",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "4fa49ff27493",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Epstein and Holt (2006)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0037",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "c107f2d5d147",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Hoffman et al.~(2016)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0043",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "00905a35d081",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The inventory contains 20 sources: nine S2\\_VERIFIED, ten VERIFIED, and one PLAUSIBLE; 18 were conservatively counted as peer reviewed. S2\\_VERIFIED establishes"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0045",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "182f58bfa1ab",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Every literature statement has a visible frozen citation and \\texttt{anchor:none}; no direct quotation is used. The recoverable workflow fields are repository-l"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0077",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "5dfc655bda88",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The frozen literature supports genus-two octagon objects, Bolza context, and candidate-generation precedents, but it does not itself identify unique primitive i"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0091",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "88633eee5336",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Validated numerical methods may support cutoff or sign predicates where their hypotheses apply. Johansson (2017)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0106",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "9757770c80d4",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Second, locator-level support remains materially incomplete. All 48 literature uses carry anchor:none. Exact page, section, paragraph, or quotation passages wer"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0007",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "36066564a7f8",
      "first_line_excerpt": "This report asks what exact-certificate architecture could eventually support primitive-geodesic ownership decisions for a source-locked Bolza surface and one f"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0010",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "c96a54aac5fd",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section*{{\\cjkfont 繁\\hspace{0pt}體\\hspace{0pt}中\\hspace{0pt}文\\hspace{0pt}摘\\hspace{0pt}要\\hspace{0pt}}}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0020",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "512a0f15dddc",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The inherited cutoff was historically target-blind, but its coarse support implication is now known. The source-locked target inequality places the Bolza side b"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0073",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "7561adb417bc",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The contract also separates local record validity from population completeness. A conjugacy witness may be correct for one pair while the candidate universe is "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0100",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "2c1d5fda7edb",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The frozen target-control pair remains useful as an interface stress test because its representations may demand different proof routes. It is not presently a c"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0109",
      "operation": "replace_block",
      "old_hash": "1dc16ad56b86",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Fifth, the frozen scientific design is asymmetric and limited. The target's below-cutoff emptiness is largely an inherited replay, while nontrivial closure lies"
    }
  ],
